# 10. Data Storage

## DynamoDB (Operational)

Tables:

### Proposals

Partition Key:

proposal_id

Attributes:

total_votes
option_counts (updated from `VoteRevealed` only; empty or hidden until `results_visible`)
status / phase (commit | reveal | finalized | closed)
commit_ends_at
reveal_ends_at
results_visible (bool; true after reveal phase ends / finalized)
updated_at
electorate_merkle_root (optional; frozen at proposal open, Phase 3)
electorate_registry_version (optional)
electorate_snapshot_slot (optional)

### EligibilityAudit (optional, Phase 3)

Append-only projection of eligibility events for transparency queries (partition key e.g. `event_id` or `timestamp` + sort key).

---

### VoterActivity

Partition Key:

voter_pubkey

Attributes:

has_committed (per proposal; from VoteCommitted)
has_revealed (per proposal; from VoteRevealed)
last_commit_timestamp
last_reveal_timestamp

---

## BigQuery (Analytics)

Tables:

### votes_raw

Columns:

proposal_id
option_id
voter_pubkey
timestamp
slot
tx_signature
event_type (VoteRevealed for tally; VoteCommitted for participation analytics)
commitment (for VoteCommitted rows)

---

### proposal_trends

Columns:

proposal_id
window_start
votes_per_minute
voter_growth_rate
anomaly_flag

---

### eligibility_events (Phase 3)

Append-only audit log mirrored from chain events:

event_id
event_type
timestamp
slot
merkle_root (for EligibleVotersRootUpdated)
registry_version
voter_pubkey (for grant/revoke)
proposal_id (when linked, e.g. snapshot reference)

Supports retroactive queries: global add/remove timeline; electorate pinned per proposal via `ProposalCreated` fields in `votes_raw` or a `proposals` dimension table.

